Rohan Anil notes that the field has produced many Adam variants, mainly overfitting CIFAR and ImageNet, leading to confusion. This is why AlgoPerf competitions were organized to benchmark training algorithms.

@YifeiZuoX highlights that recent optimizer records tuned for Attention do not transfer well to PLX, and identifies two promising modifications: Hyperball and EMA-Nesterov. Under parameter-matched settings, PLX achieves notable results, as shown in the accompanying images.

The MLCommons AlgoPerf benchmark measures how much faster neural network training can be achieved by changing the training algorithm, aiming to improve efficiency.

